From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bastiaan van der Plaat <bastiaan.v.d.plaat@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 12:18:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Nintendo DS build

Makefile.nds builds a .nds with the toolchain of the ports (clang,
calico and libnds), with the Apogee v1.4 graphics layout, the game data
from NITRO_DIR embedded through NitroFS and ICON as the icon. The ray
caster, the scaler and the fixed point math run from ITCM as ARM code,
the rest is Thumb code in main RAM. Enums keep the size of an int,
savegames hold structs with them. The signon screen isn't shown, so its
64 KiB picture isn't built in, and the Tab debug keys are left out, there
is no keyboard to press them. The cold code (startup, config and
savegames, the menus, the intermission and the help texts) is optimized
for size. The screen is the 320x200 frame of 8 bits, the DS has no
sys/uio.h.
